misc: add the H713 AV1 presence probe

A read-only module that powers the AV1 domain, ungates its bus and mbus
clocks, deasserts its reset, and reports the head of its register file plus a
scan for the core ID marker.  It decodes nothing and writes nothing to the
block.

It exists to settle two questions before a real driver is worth starting:

  Is the block on this die?  Clock gates and a power domain prove the SoC
  design includes it; they do not prove this package does, and no register has
  ever been read from it.  An all-zero window is reported explicitly as NO
  RESPONSE rather than left to be misread as an idle block -- that distinction
  is the whole point of the module.

  Which register-file variant is it?  The vendor's AsicRegisterMapWidth picks
  1168 bytes (292 registers, SwRegisters) or 816 bytes (204 registers,
  BigSeaRegisters) by comparing a core ID against 0xb16c.  The scan matches on
  the low 16 bits, as the vendor does, and prints the whole word, because the
  upper half is plausibly a revision or synthesis configuration.

Built as a module on purpose.  The DT node needs a flash, but the driver does
not, so iterating on what to read costs an insmod rather than a reflash and a
cold boot.  Unloading it asserts the reset and drops the power domain again.

The reset is claimed exclusively, which is correct here: reset_av1 has no other
consumer.  The node deliberately does not ask for reset_ve, which is cedrus's.


Later extended with a debugfs replay interface (/sys/kernel/debug/h713-av1/):
it runs one frame the vendor library programmed -- register image plus the
DMA buffers its *_base fields point into, relocated to real IOVAs -- as
captured by tools/re/av1/vendor-decode.py from the library running under
emulation. On 2026-09-29 the first frame of the stock test clip decoded
BIT-EXACT through it (luma and NV12 chroma identical to libdav1d), in 1.6 ms,
once PLL_VE was brought down from cedrus's 600 MHz to stock's 432 MHz: at
600 MHz the core stalls into its own cycle timeout.
--- a/drivers/misc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/misc/Kconfig
@@ -15,6 +15,20 @@
 	  The carveout is a no-map reservation with no struct page, so the
 	  exporter uses dma_map_resource() instead of page-backed sg.
 
+config SUNXI_H713_AV1_PROBE
+	tristate "H713 AV1 decoder presence probe"
+	depends on ARCH_SUNXI || COMPILE_TEST
+	help
+	  Reads the core ID of the H713's AV1 decoder and reports it. The block
+	  is Google IP -- the stock DTB calls it "allwinner,sunxi-google-ve" --
+	  and no driver for it exists in any tree.
+
+	  This decodes nothing and writes nothing to the block. It exists to
+	  settle whether the hardware is present on this die, and which of its
+	  two register-file variants it is, before a real driver is attempted.
+
+	  Say M here if you are investigating AV1 support; otherwise say N.
+
 menu "Misc devices"
 
 config SENSORS_LIS3LV02D
--- a/drivers/misc/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/misc/Makefile
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
